# Build products, not source. Libraries/dyld/dyld/dyld is a linked dyld built
# from this tree; it was checked in by mistake and carries absolute host paths
# (/Users/max/Projects/build/...) in its debug strings. It is ours, not Apple's,
# but it is a build artifact and must never be committed. The Apple-derived
# payload that genuinely must not be published is policed separately, in
# tools/bootlab/assets/.gitignore.
#
# NOTE: deliberately no blanket *.o / *.d rule. 1363 .o files are tracked in
# this repository, including unit-test fixtures under
# Libraries/dyld/unit-tests/test-cases/, so a global object-file ignore would
# hide real fixtures.
/Libraries/dyld/dyld/dyld

# The bootlab asset tree. Every file under it except this directory's own
# .gitignore is an Apple product binary, a third-party EFI binary, or a
# regenerable build artifact of this project. Measured 2026-09-28: 45 Apple
# product binaries totalling 11,626,528 bytes. The detailed, per-file
# provenance record is in tools/bootlab/assets/.gitignore, which IS tracked.
#
# The files stay on disk. boot.efi in particular is load-bearing: the boot
# path is host OVMF -> UEFI Shell -> the typed command
# fs0:\System\Library\CoreServices\boot.efi. Ignoring a path does not remove
# it from the working tree, so the lab keeps working while nothing is
# committed.
/tools/bootlab/assets/*
!/tools/bootlab/assets/.gitignore
